ness_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"eCikDKFbaeYVNdCD2beX0Q","review_id":"74JpIyVD5WBbomAuHkGfLw","date":"2018-03-22T12:49:16","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9464477896690369,"text_excerpt":"A lively, casual place to nosh in between taking in some jazz on Frenchman! It's one of the only eateries mixed in with a bunch of bars so it can definitely get crowded when the drunkin' munchies hit. We came before closing at midnight and there was still a wait! We heard from some locals say this is the place to go for good times, brews and great dogs. The fact that they have not one, but three veg options had me sold! They also have crawfish sausage, a dog made with Guinness, gator, duck, bratwurst, kielbasa and a creole dog too. Torn between the three vegan dogs, Spicy Chipotle Dog ,Field Roast Italian Dog and Smoked Apple Sage, I wound up going for a chipotle dog. I decided to top my ..."},{"business_id":"eCikDKFbaeYVNdCD2beX0Q","review_id":"Q3jMRzN4fJvfExy8ahFYJA","date":"2018-05-30T04:18:16","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9453357458114624,"text_excerpt":"Dat Dog is dat place to be when you're on Frenchman street. Our group of 10 came here before going out to watch the Warriors/Rockets game and we were lucky to nab a table upstairs. Dat Dog is separated into two floors with the bottom floor being the main kitchen/bar and the upstairs being the balcony/bar as well. The downstairs area was much hotter than the upstairs, go figure so if I were you I would try to grab a table upstairs because they also have tables outside and multiple bathrooms. This place has a solid selection of dogs and additional toppings that start at ~$8. I ended up getting the polish kielbasa and it was delicious. It was cooked well and had a nice snap. What was even be..."},{"business_id":"eCikDKFbaeYVNdCD2beX0Q","review_id":"Jzumu13JRZDrDjw7aTC5VA","date":"2016-12-05T01:26:04","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9452724456787109,"text_excerpt":"First thing ya need to know is that the location is in an amazing location, surrounded by great live music bands, Dat Dog is open and making some great foodage later than everyone else in the area. The vibe is awesome, great mix of tourists and locals. Second thing is everything is in the form of a hot dog. I didn't know that but was surprised when I opened my food box (I got the order to go). And had a hamburger dog with all the fixins. Thats another thing - at this place you can get just about ANYTHING on your dog (burger, hot or chicken). Bartender was great - attentive and very nice suggesting a few other places to try while we were in town. Wish he had mentioned trying the second flo..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"eCikDKFbaeYVNdCD2beX0Q","photo_id":"3pv03aKLjysxNO8uKVwHtA","label":"menu","image_url":"/photos/3pv03aKLjysxNO8uKVwHtA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8947967290878296},{"business_id":"eCikDKFbaeYVNdCD2beX0Q","photo_id":"Imk60sE1M9SiAw1Jb8ck2g","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/Imk60sE1M9SiAw1J